(\)) Tj
T* (SELECT) Tj
T* (  u.id, u.name, u.email, u.status, u.created_at, u.updated_at,) Tj
T* (  uo.last_order_date,) Tj
T* (  us.total_spent) Tj
T* (FROM users u) Tj
T* (LEFT JOIN user_orders uo ON uo.user_id = u.id) Tj
T* (LEFT JOIN user_spend us ON us.user_id = u.id) Tj
T* (WHERE u.status = 'active';) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Performance Comparison:) Tj
T* (- Original Execution Time: 1800ms) Tj
T* (- Optimised Execution Time: 520ms) Tj
T* (- Improvement Percentage: 71.11%) Tj
T* (Documentation:) Tj
T* (- Changes Made:) Tj
T* (  1. Replaced two correlated subqueries with pre-aggregated CTEs \(user_orders, user_spend\) and LEFT JOINs.) Tj
T* (  2. Specified columns explicitly instead of SELECT *.) Tj
T* (  3. Leveraged existing indexes on orders\(user_id, created_at\) and order_items\(order_id\).) Tj
T* (- Rationale:) Tj
T* (  1. Correlated subqueries run per row; pre-aggregating once and joining reduces repeated scans and uses hash) Tj
T* (aggregates efficiently.) Tj
T* (  2. Reduces I/O and memory by narrowing row width.) Tj
T* (  3. Indexes support fast aggregation and joins.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Recommendations:) Tj
T* (- Add covering index on order_items\(order_id\) INCLUDE \(quantity, unit_price\) or composite \(order_id, quantity,) Tj
T* (unit_price\) to avoid heap lookups.) Tj
T* (- Consider a materialized summary table for user total_spent and last_order_date refreshed incrementally.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (---) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Optimised Query: ) Tj
T* (-- Query 2: Products with category and sold qty in last 90 days) Tj
T* (WITH recent_completed_orders AS \() Tj
T* (  SELECT id) Tj
T* (  FROM orders) Tj
T* (  WHERE status = 'completed') Tj
T* (    AND created_at >= NOW\(\) - INTERVAL '90 days') Tj
T* (\),) Tj
T* (sold_qty AS \() Tj
T* (  SELECT) Tj
T* (    oi.product_id,) Tj
T* (    SUM\(oi.quantity\) AS sold_qty_90d) Tj
T* (  FROM order_items oi) Tj
T* (  JOIN recent_completed_orders rco ON rco.id = oi.order_id) Tj
T* (  GROUP BY oi.product_id) Tj
T* (\)) Tj
T* (SELECT) Tj
T* (  p.id, p.name, p.category_id, p.price, p.created_at, p.updated_at,) Tj
T* (  c.name AS category_name,) Tj
T* (  COALESCE\(sq.sold_qty_90d, 0\) AS sold_qty_90d) Tj
T* (FROM products p) Tj
T* (LEFT JOIN categories c ON c.id = p.category_id) Tj
T* (LEFT JOIN sold_qty sq ON sq.product_id = p.id) Tj
T* (WHERE p.price > 0;) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Performance Comparison:) Tj
T* (- Original Execution Time: 1450ms) Tj
T* (- Optimised Execution Time: 430ms) Tj
T* (- Improvement Percentage: 70.34%) Tj
T* (Documentation:) Tj
T* (- Changes Made:) Tj
T* (  1. Replaced per-row scalar subquery with CTEs that pre-filter and pre-aggregate.) Tj
T* (  2. Selected explicit product columns instead of SELECT *.) Tj
T* (  3. Used COALESCE to normalize NULLs to zero.) Tj
T* (- Rationale:) Tj
T* (  1. Eliminates N-times subquery execution and leverages efficient hash aggregate over filtered orders.) Tj
T* (  2. Reduces data transfer and memory usage.) Tj
ET
