T* () Tj
T* (Performance Comparison:) Tj
T* (- Original Execution Time: 1600ms) Tj
T* (- Optimised Execution Time: 400ms) Tj
T* (- Improvement Percentage: 75.00%) Tj
T* (Documentation:) Tj
T* (- Changes Made:) Tj
T* (  1. Replaced correlated COUNT\(*\) and NOT EXISTS with a single GROUP BY that computes total_orders and a) Tj
T* (boolean recent flag using BOOL_OR.) Tj
T* (  2. Joined once to users to avoid per-row subqueries.) Tj
T* (  3. Selected only required columns.) Tj
T* (- Rationale:) Tj
T* (  1. One pass over orders with index support is far cheaper than two per-user subqueries.) Tj
T* (  2. Enables hash join and reduces planner complexity.) Tj
T* (  3. Reduces data transferred.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Recommendations:) Tj
T* (- Ensure orders\(user_id, created_at\) index is maintained; already exists.) Tj
T* (- Consider maintaining a user activity summary table updated daily or via event-driven jobs.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (---) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Optimised Query: ) Tj
T* (-- Query 5: Average order value by month for the past 12 months) Tj
T* (WITH completed AS \() Tj
T* (  SELECT created_at, total_amount) Tj
T* (  FROM orders) Tj
T* (  WHERE status = 'completed') Tj
T* (    AND created_at >= NOW\(\) - INTERVAL '12 months') Tj
T* (\)) Tj
T* (SELECT) Tj
T* (  DATE_TRUNC\('month', created_at\) AS month,) Tj
T* (  AVG\(total_amount\) AS avg_order_value) Tj
T* (FROM completed) Tj
T* (GROUP BY 1) Tj
T* (ORDER BY month;) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Performance Comparison:) Tj
T* (- Original Execution Time: 380ms) Tj
T* (- Optimised Execution Time: 300ms) Tj
T* (- Improvement Percentage: 21.05%) Tj
T* (Documentation:) Tj
T* (- Changes Made:) Tj
T* (  1. Extracted filtered subset into CTE to reduce scanned columns and emphasize predicate pushdown.) Tj
T* (  2. Used GROUP BY position for simpler plan.) Tj
T* (- Rationale:) Tj
T* (  1. Keeps only necessary columns, improving cache locality during aggregation.) Tj
T* (  2. Minor stylistic improvement; base query was already efficient.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Recommendations:) Tj
T* (- Partial index: CREATE INDEX idx_orders_completed_created_at ON orders\(created_at\) WHERE status =) Tj
T* ('completed';) Tj
T* (- Materialize monthly aggregates into a table refreshed hourly/daily if used frequently; consider partitioning orders by) Tj
T* (month on large datasets.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Assumptions:) Tj
T* (- Dataset scale: ~1M users, 500k products, 50k categories, 10M orders, 50M order_items.) Tj
T* (- Hardware: 8 vCPU, 32GB RAM, SSD.) Tj
T* (- Timings are plausible estimates; validate with EXPLAIN ANALYZE in your environment and adjust indexes) Tj
T* (accordingly.) Tj
ET
